+# Small-amount triangle experiment — 2026-09-10
+
+Parent: 7abaae9902dc0b7d7579c66795885fada6e85a43, successful run 34476200641.
+
+The parent checked 0.001, 0.01, 0.1 and 1 WETH. Four route families had
+positive marginal bounds, but all fourteen successful quotes were negative;
+two 1-WETH calls reverted. That is not proof about smaller amounts.
+
+This experiment adds 0.000001, 0.00001, 0.00005, 0.0001, 0.0002 and
+0.0005 WETH. The maximum number of discrete route/amount combinations is
+1280 (two directions, four fee choices per leg, ten amounts). These are
+sample points, not a continuous optimum or a proof about every loan size.
+
+At most 64 exact Quoter calls per provider remain allowed after bound pruning.
+Unquoted or reverted candidates remain explicitly unresolved. Pool allowlists,
+EIP-1898 block hashes, source/evidence checksums, two-provider state agreement,
+local chain ID 31337, treasury accounting, baseline preservation, and the ban
+on signing/broadcasting public transactions are unchanged.
+
+Every size is a multiple of 10000 base units; multiplying by any integer-bps
+premium is exact. This does not establish that every future Aave deployment
+uses the same rounding rule for arbitrary sizes.
+
+The source-level Python and Solidity allowlists are tested for agreement.
+The matched-fork harness uses the same ten-size allowlist and executes only
+screen-selected candidates (maximum three), with zero prefund and local
+prefund preservation tests. Other quotes are not fork-verified automatically.
+
+Gross surplus, if any, is before the full Arbitrum execution and data fee.
+The harness sets a one-wei gas-budget placeholder solely to test the economic
+repayment threshold. This is NOT a real fee estimate; no live execution is
+allowed and no simulated surplus is recorded as earnings.
+
+Background: https://docs.arbitrum.io/arbitrum-essentials/how-to-estimate-gas
